<li id="A4.I8.i14" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">14.</span> 
<div id="A4.I8.i14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I8.i14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I8.i14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{S}_{3}:={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{s}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}-\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{s}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]={\bm{u}}_{\beta}(I-{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}){\bm{b}}{\bm{a}}^{\top}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{S}_{3}:={\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{s}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}-\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{s}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]={\bm{u}}_{\beta}(I-{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}){\bm{b}}{\bm{a}}^{\top}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I8.i15" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">15.</span> 
<div id="A4.I8.i15.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I8.i15.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.I8.i15.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{S}_{4}:={\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}-\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]={\bm{b}}^{\top}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{a}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>S</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒂</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{S}_{4}:={\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}-\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]={\bm{b}}^{\top}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{a}}</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Hence we see that these are all homogeneous polynomials in uniformly random spherical variables. Thus, we can use Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma14" title="Lemma 14 (Product Spherical Hypercontractivity). ‣ D.4.2 Step 3(b): Bounding the Higher Moments ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>, we get bounds on the higher moments. In particular, since the coefficients are only dependent on constants and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that the coefficients are independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{a}},{\bm{b}},{\bm{u}}_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒂</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒖</mi><mi>β</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{a}},{\bm{b}},{\bm{u}}_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then using a change of basis we see that that coefficients of the decomposition are also random and independent of the input variables. Finally, since the spectrum converges to the Marchenko-Pastur, we have that the coefficients have bounded moments. Hence the second assumption is satisfied.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS4.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.4.3 </span>Step 3(c): Bounding <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> moments.</h4>

<div id="Thmlemma16" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma16.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 16</span></span><span id="Thmlemma16.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Moments of <math id="Thmlemma16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}/\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}/\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma16.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I9" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I9.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I9.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I9.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I9.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I9.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex189" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex189.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I9.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I9.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I9.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I9.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I9.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{2}/\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{2}/\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I9.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex190" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex190.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">We decompose</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex191" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex191.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}=\zeta_{i}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}},\quad i=1,2,\quad\text{where }\zeta_{1}=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2},\quad\zeta_{2}=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mtext>where </mtext><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>ζ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}=\zeta_{i}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}},\quad i=1,2,\quad\text{where }\zeta_{1}=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2},\quad\zeta_{2}=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Expectation Estimates:</span> We begin by noting that <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}},{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}},{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}},{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}},{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Additionally, <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Also <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depends on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>, hence is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we have have that <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent. Thus, we see that</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.Ex192" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex192.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\zeta_{1}]=\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}]\;\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\zeta_{1}]=\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]=\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}]\;\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> again,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex193" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex193.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}]=1-c,\quad\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]=\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}]=1-c,\quad\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]=\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We plug them into the expectation and get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex194" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex194.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\zeta_{1}]=\left(1-c\right)\left[\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right]=\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\zeta_{1}]=\left(1-c\right)\left[\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right]=\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, we also have that from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex195" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex195.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex196" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex196.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\mathbb{E}[\zeta_{1}]+\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\mathbb{E}[\zeta_{1}]+\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]=\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">A similar argument applies for <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{2}/\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{2}/\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, using the corresponding results for <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variance Estimates:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Again using independence, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx43" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex197"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex197.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex197.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2})\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}]^{2}\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]^{2}\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2})\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}]^{2}\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]^{2}\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex198"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex198.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\,O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)+(1-c)^{2}\,O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)+\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c^{2}}{(1-c)^{2}}\,O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\,O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)+(1-c)^{2}\,O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)+\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c^{2}}{(1-c)^{2}}\,O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex199"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex199.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">We then use Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma34" title="Lemma 34 (Variance of a sum). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> to compute the variance of the sum:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex200"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex200.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\zeta_{1}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\zeta_{1}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex200.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}(\zeta_{1})}+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}(\zeta_{1})}+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex201"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex201.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\sqrt{O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)}+\sqrt{O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)}\right)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\sqrt{O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)}+\sqrt{O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)}\right)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex202"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex202.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p6.3.1" class="ltx_text">This proof is similar to the other case.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma17" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 17</span></span><span id="Thmlemma17.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Moments of <math id="Thmlemma17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\gamma_{i}/\eta^{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\gamma_{i}/\eta^{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma17.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma17.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma17.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma17.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have, as <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,d\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,d\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmlemma17.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d/n\to c\neq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d/n\to c\neq 1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I10" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I10.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I10.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I10.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I10.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I10.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I10.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex203" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex203.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right]=\left(\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\;+\;O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right),\qquad\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right)=O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}\,n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right]=\left(\frac{c}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\;+\;O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right),\qquad\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right)=O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}\,n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I10.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I10.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I10.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I10.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I10.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{2}/\eta^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{2}/\eta^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I10.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex204" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex204.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right]=\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\;+\;O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right),\qquad\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\left(\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right)=O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}\,n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.497em;" width="0.497em"><mi>𝔼</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.502em">+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\!\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right]=\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\;+\;O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right),\qquad\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\left(\frac{\gamma_{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)^{\!2}\right)=O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}\,n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Write, for <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in\{1,2\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in\{1,2\}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex205" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex205.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}=\zeta_{i}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}},\qquad\zeta_{1}:=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2},\ \ \zeta_{2}:=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ζ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}=\zeta_{i}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}},\qquad\zeta_{1}:=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2},\ \ \zeta_{2}:=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\,\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Means.<span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 (Moments of 𝛾_𝑖/𝜂^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> and the fact that for any random variable</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex206" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex206.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[Y^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}[Y]^{2}+\mathrm{Var}(Y)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[Y^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}[Y]^{2}+\mathrm{Var}(Y)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">we get the means.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Variances.<span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Using</span></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex207" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex207.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y^{2}=\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]^{2}+2(\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right])\left(Y-\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]\right)+\left(Y-\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]\right)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y^{2}=\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]^{2}+2(\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right])\left(Y-\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]\right)+\left(Y-\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma34" title="Lemma 34 (Variance of a sum). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">34</span></a> we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex208" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex208.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(Y^{2})\leq\left(\sqrt{4\left(\mathbb{E}\left[X\right]\right)^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}(X_{i})}\ +\ \sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\left(Y-\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]\right)^{2}\right)}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.722em" rspace="0.722em">+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.643em;" width="1.643em"><mi>Var</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(Y^{2})\leq\left(\sqrt{4\left(\mathbb{E}\left[X\right]\right)^{2}\,\mathrm{Var}(X_{i})}\ +\ \sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\!\left(\left(Y-\mathbb{E}\left[Y\right]\right)^{2}\right)}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">By spherical hypercontractivity for degree-<math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math> polynomials,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex209" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex209.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}-\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right]\right)^{4}\right]\lesssim\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right)^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}-\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right]\right)^{4}\right]\lesssim\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right)^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">hence</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex210" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex210.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left(\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}-\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right]\right)^{2}\right)\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}-\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right]\right)^{4}\right]\lesssim\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≲</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left(\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}-\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right]\right)^{2}\right)\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}-\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right]\right)^{4}\right]\lesssim\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}\right]^{2}=O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}\right]^{2}=O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O(\rho^{-4}n^{-1})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}}{\eta^{2}}\right)=O(\rho^{-4}n^{-1})</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex211" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex211.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right)=O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{i}^{2}}{\eta^{4}}\right)=O\!\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">as claimed.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma18" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma18.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 18</span></span><span id="Thmlemma18.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Finite Negative Moments of <math id="Thmlemma18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma18.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma18.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma18.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma18.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Fix <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. There exists an <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N(p)</annotation></semantics></math> such that for all <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,d\geq N(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,d\geq N(p)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that for <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex212" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex212.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\gamma_{1}^{-p}\right]\leq\eta^{-2p}\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[T^{-p}\right]\leq\frac{\rho^{2p}}{\eta^{2p}}\,M^{p}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\gamma_{1}^{-p}\right]\leq\eta^{-2p}\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[T^{-p}\right]\leq\frac{\rho^{2p}}{\eta^{2p}}\,M^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma18.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma18.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and for <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex213" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex213.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\gamma_{2}^{-p}\right]\leq\eta^{-2p}\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[S^{-p}\right]\leq\frac{\rho^{2p}}{\eta^{2p}}\\
,M^{p}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\gamma_{2}^{-p}\right]\leq\eta^{-2p}\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[S^{-p}\right]\leq\frac{\rho^{2p}}{\eta^{2p}}\\
,M^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma18.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma18.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is the largest singular value of <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T:=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\sim Beta\left(\frac{n-d}{2},\frac{d}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐭</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\sim Beta\left(\frac{n-d}{2},\frac{d}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="Thmlemma18.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\sim Beta\left(\frac{d-n}{2},\frac{n}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐬</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\sim Beta\left(\frac{d-n}{2},\frac{n}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">Recall our SVD <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> and that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex214" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex214.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}\quad\text{ and }\quad\gamma_{2}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}\quad\text{ and }\quad\gamma_{2}=\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}+\xi^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex215" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex215.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{{\bm{b}}_{i}^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\geq\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{b}}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\frac{{\bm{b}}_{i}^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\geq\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{b}}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex216" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex216.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{{\bm{a}}_{i}^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\geq\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{a}}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mfrac><msubsup><mi>𝒂</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒂</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\frac{{\bm{a}}_{i}^{2}}{\sigma_{i}^{2}}\geq\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{a}}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p9.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we see that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex217" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex217.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{1}\geq\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\quad\text{ and }\quad\gamma_{2}\geq\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{1}\geq\eta^{2}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}\quad\text{ and }\quad\gamma_{2}\geq\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\frac{1}{\sigma_{1}^{2}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text"> depends only on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑽</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}},{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}},{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{V}},{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝚺</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{V}},{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math>. <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\Sigma}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝚺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\Sigma}}</annotation></semantics></math> and is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}},{\bm{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑽</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}},{\bm{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> is independent of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T:=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T:=\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p10.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S:=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>:=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S:=\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, we get that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex218" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex218.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{\gamma_{1}^{p}}\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2p}}{\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2p}}\quad\text{ and }\quad\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{p}}\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2p}}{\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2p}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{\gamma_{1}^{p}}\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2p}}{\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2p}}\quad\text{ and }\quad\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{p}}\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\frac{\sigma_{1}^{2p}}{\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2p}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p11.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p11.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then taking the expectation and using the independence, we get that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex219" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex219.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{1}^{p}}\right]\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\,\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2p}}\right]\,\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{p}}\right]\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\,\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2p}}\right]\,\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{1}^{p}}\right]\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\,\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2p}}\right]\,\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{p}}\right]\leq\frac{1}{\eta^{2p}}\,\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2p}}\right]\,\mathbb{E}\left[\sigma_{1}^{2p}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&lt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&lt;n</annotation></semantics></math>), the right null space of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> (dimension <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n-d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n-d</annotation></semantics></math>) is a uniformly random <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(n-d)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(n-d)</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional subspace of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>. The squared norm <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the squared length of the projection of the fixed unit vector <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{v}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{v}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> onto this random subspace. The distribution of such a squared projection norm is <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Beta}\left(\frac{n-d}{2},\frac{d}{2}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Beta}\left(\frac{n-d}{2},\frac{d}{2}\right)</annotation></semantics></math>, as it can be represented as the ratio of two independent chi-squared random variables: <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{n-d}G_{i}^{2}/\sum_{i=1}^{n}G_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">/</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{n-d}G_{i}^{2}/\sum_{i=1}^{n}G_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{i}{\sim}N(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{i}{\sim}N(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> IID, which follows the desired Beta distribution. Similarly for <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p12.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the eigenvalue distribution converges to the compactly supported distribution. We can see that for sufficiently large <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n,d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n,d</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that there exists an <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{1}\leq\rho M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{1}\leq\rho M</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y\sim\mathrm{Beta}(\alpha,\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>Beta</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y\sim\mathrm{Beta}(\alpha,\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p&lt;\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p&lt;\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex220" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex220.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[Y^{-p}]=\frac{\Gamma(\alpha-p)\,\Gamma(\alpha+\beta)}{\Gamma(\alpha)\,\Gamma(\alpha+\beta-p)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>α</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[Y^{-p}]=\frac{\Gamma(\alpha-p)\,\Gamma(\alpha+\beta)}{\Gamma(\alpha)\,\Gamma(\alpha+\beta-p)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, using Stirling on the <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math> ratio,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex221" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex221.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[T^{-p}]\to_{n,d\to\infty}\left(\frac{\alpha_{1}+\beta_{1}}{\alpha_{1}}\right)^{p}=\left(\frac{1}{1-c}\right)^{p}\quad(c&lt;1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>T</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[T^{-p}]\to_{n,d\to\infty}\left(\frac{\alpha_{1}+\beta_{1}}{\alpha_{1}}\right)^{p}=\left(\frac{1}{1-c}\right)^{p}\quad(c&lt;1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex222" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex222.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[S^{-p}]\to_{n,d\to\infty}\left(\frac{\alpha_{2}+\beta_{2}}{\alpha_{2}}\right)^{p}=\left(\frac{c}{c-1}\right)^{p}\quad(c&gt;1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>S</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><msub><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[S^{-p}]\to_{n,d\to\infty}\left(\frac{\alpha_{2}+\beta_{2}}{\alpha_{2}}\right)^{p}=\left(\frac{c}{c-1}\right)^{p}\quad(c&gt;1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, there is an <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex223" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex223.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{1}^{p}}\right]\leq\left(\frac{\rho}{\eta}\right)^{2p}\,M^{p}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{p}}\right]\leq\left(\frac{\rho}{\eta}\right)^{2p}\,M^{p}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi></msubsup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{1}^{p}}\right]\leq\left(\frac{\rho}{\eta}\right)^{2p}\,M^{p}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{p}}\right]\leq\left(\frac{\rho}{\eta}\right)^{2p}\,M^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p15" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p15.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p15.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma19" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma19.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 19</span></span><span id="Thmlemma19.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Moments of <math id="Thmlemma19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}/\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}/\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma19.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma19.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma19.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma19.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I11" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I11.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I11.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I11.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I11.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I11.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}/\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}/\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I11.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex224" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex224.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I11.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I11.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I11.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I11.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I11.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}/\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}/\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I11.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex225" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex225.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma32" title="Lemma 32. ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">32</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 (Moments of 𝛾_𝑖/𝜂^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, the expectation of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}/\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}/\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed by:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx45" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex226"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex226.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}]}1+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}d}\right)=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}]}1+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}d}\right)=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma33" title="Lemma 33 (Variance of a reciprocal). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 (Moments of 𝛾_𝑖/𝜂^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>, the variance of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}/\gamma_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}/\gamma_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed by:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx46" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex227"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex227.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex227.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}]^{4}}O\left(\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)\right)+o\left(\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\mathbb{E}[\gamma_{1}/\eta^{2}]^{4}}O\left(\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)\right)+o\left(\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\gamma_{1}}{\eta^{2}}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex228"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex228.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\rho^{8}\eta^{8}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{4}}O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>8</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\rho^{8}\eta^{8}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{4}}O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex229"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex229.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\quad\text{by the scalings of $\eta$ and $\rho$}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>by the scalings of </mtext><mi>η</mi><mtext> and </mtext><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\quad\text{by the scalings of $\eta$ and $\rho$}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p16.3.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is similar for the other term.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma20" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma20.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 20</span></span><span id="Thmlemma20.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Moments of <math id="Thmlemma20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{4}/\gamma_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{4}/\gamma_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma20.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma20.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma20.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma20.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">We have:</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I12" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I12.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(i)</span> 
<div id="A4.I12.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I12.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I12.ix1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I12.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{4}/\gamma_{1}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{4}/\gamma_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I12.ix1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex230" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex230.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I12.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(ii)</span> 
<div id="A4.I12.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I12.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I12.ix2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I12.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{4}/\gamma_{2}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{4}/\gamma_{2}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I12.ix2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex231" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex231.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(1\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(1\right),\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.6" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">The expectation of <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{4}/\gamma_{1}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{4}/\gamma_{1}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> can be computed by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma19" title="Lemma 19 (Moments of 𝜂^2/𝛾_𝑖). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>. By definition we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex232"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex232.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]=\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]\right)^{2}+\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)=\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)^{2}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]=\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]\right)^{2}+\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)=\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)^{2}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.2.1" class="ltx_text">The variance follows Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma33" title="Lemma 33 (Variance of a reciprocal). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">33</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma17" title="Lemma 17 (Moments of (𝛾_𝑖/𝜂^2)^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx48" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex233"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex233.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.3.1" class="ltx_text">since the mean is <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p17.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p18" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p18.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p18.1.1" class="ltx_text">The proof is similar for the other term.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma21" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma21.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 21</span></span><span id="Thmlemma21.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma21.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma21.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma21.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="Thmlemma21.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝛆</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> whose entries have mean <math id="Thmlemma21.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>, variance <math id="Thmlemma21.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>, and follow our noise assumptions. Then for any indepedent random matrix <math id="Thmlemma21.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{Q}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{Q}}\in\mathbb{R}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex234" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex234.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\varepsilon}},{\bm{Q}}}\left[{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{Q}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right]=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Tr({\bm{Q}})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑸</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜺</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\varepsilon}},{\bm{Q}}}\left[{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{Q}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right]=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Tr({\bm{Q}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.7" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p19" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">We have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex235" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex235.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{Q}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\varepsilon_{i}\varepsilon_{j}Q_{ij}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜺</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{Q}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\sum_{j=1}^{n}\varepsilon_{i}\varepsilon_{j}Q_{ij}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p20" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p20.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p20.1.1" class="ltx_text">We take the expectation of this sum. By the independence assumption and assumption <math id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i}\varepsilon_{j}]=0\ \text{when}\ i\neq j" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>when</mtext><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\varepsilon_{i}\varepsilon_{j}]=0\ \text{when}\ i\neq j</annotation></semantics></math>, we then have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex236" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex236.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\varepsilon}},{\bm{Q}}}\left[{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{Q}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\left[\varepsilon_{i}^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[Q_{ii}\right]=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}Q_{ii}\right]=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Tr({\bm{Q}})\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑸</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝜺</mi></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>Tr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑸</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{{\bm{\varepsilon}},{\bm{Q}}}\left[{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{Q}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\left[\varepsilon_{i}^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[Q_{ii}\right]=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\sum_{i=1}^{n}Q_{ii}\right]=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\Tr({\bm{Q}})\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p20.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS4.SSS3.p20.2.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms</h3>

<div id="A4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Section <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Step 1: Decompose Error ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a> we decomposed the error into four terms – Bias, Variance, Data Noise and Target alignment. In Section <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>, we wrote each of these terms as the sum and product of various “elementary building blocks”. In Section <a href="#A4.SS4" title="D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4</span></a>, we should that these elementary building blocks concentrate. In this section, since we have tight concentration (i.e., the higher moment bounds). We can use Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma36" title="Lemma 36 (Variance of general product). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, which shows that the expectation of the product can be approximated by the product of the expectations. In this section, we do that calculation for our different terms.</p>
</div>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.1 </span>Step 4: Bias</h4>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We begin with the bias term. Recall that for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the expected bias by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma5" title="Lemma 5 (Bias Term). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> is equal to</p>
<table id="A4.Ex237" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex237.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\textbf{Bias}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left[\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}\right]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Bias</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\textbf{Bias}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left[\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}\right],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the cross term equals <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> due to <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> having mean zero entries. These two remaining expectations are given by Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma22" title="Lemma 22. ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma23" title="Lemma 23 (Expectations involving 𝑝_1 and 𝑝_2). ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>, informally via:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex238" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex238.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_term_one}}\ \ +\ \ \tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:p_expectation}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma22" title="Lemma 22. ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a></mtext></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mo>+</mo><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma23" title="Lemma 23 (Expectations involving 𝑝_1 and 𝑝_2). ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_term_one}}\ \ +\ \ \tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:p_expectation}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can plug in the value to get that the expected first term is given by</p>
<table id="A4.Ex239" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex239.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">and the second is given by</p>
<table id="A4.Ex240" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex240.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p1.5" class="ltx_p">Adding them, we then have the desired result:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex241" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex241.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\tilde{n}}\left(\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\,\frac{c}{1-c}\,\frac{1}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\right)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n^{2}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\tilde{n}}\left(\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\,\frac{c}{1-c}\,\frac{1}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}\right)+o\left(\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\right)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we instead have the following expanson:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex242" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex242.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\underbrace{{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}}_{{\bm{t}}_{1}}-\underbrace{\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}}_{{\bm{t}}_{2}}+\underbrace{\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}}_{{\bm{t}}_{3}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></munder><mo>−</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></munder></mrow><mo>+</mo><munder><munder accentunder="true"><mrow><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="true">⏟</mo></munder><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></munder></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\underbrace{{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}}_{{\bm{t}}_{1}}-\underbrace{\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}}_{{\bm{t}}_{2}}+\underbrace{\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}}_{{\bm{t}}_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">The bias equals the expectation of the norm of this vector. Taking the Frobenius norm, we have the six terms. Among the cross-terms, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\bm{t}}_{1},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\bm{t}}_{1},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\langle{\bm{t}}_{2},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\langle{\bm{t}}_{2},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle</annotation></semantics></math> have zero mean since <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{t}}_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{t}}_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\varepsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝜺</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\varepsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math> whose entries have mean <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math>. We now look at the other terms</p>
<table id="A4.EGx49" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex243"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex243.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{t}}_{3}\|^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{t}}_{3}\|^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex243.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}\right]\quad\text{by Lemma \ref{lem:eQe}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mrow><mtext>by Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma21" title="Lemma 21. ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}\right]\quad\text{by Lemma \ref{lem:eQe}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">The expectation is given by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma23" title="Lemma 23 (Expectations involving 𝑝_1 and 𝑝_2). ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a>. Subsequently, Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma22" title="Lemma 22. ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma25" title="Lemma 25. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a> give <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{1}\||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{1}\||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{2}\||^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{2}\||^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\langle{\bm{t}}_{1},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\langle{\bm{t}}_{1},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle]</annotation></semantics></math> respectively. Informally, we can compute the bias via:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx50" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex244"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex244.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\textbf{Bias}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_bold">Bias</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}[\textbf{Bias}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex244.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}-\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}}{\eta}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}{\bm{p}}_{2}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex245"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex245.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{1}\||^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{2}\||^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{3}\||^{2}]-2\mathbb{E}[\langle{\bm{t}}_{1},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle^{2}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟨</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝒕</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">⟩</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{1}\||^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{2}\||^{2}]+\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{t}}_{3}\||^{2}]-2\mathbb{E}[\langle{\bm{t}}_{1},{\bm{t}}_{3}\rangle^{2}]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex246"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex246.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_term_one}}+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\text{Lemma \ref{lem:p_expectation}}+\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_norm_2}}-2\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_zero_exp}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma22" title="Lemma 22. ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">22</span></a></mtext></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma23" title="Lemma 23 (Expectations involving 𝑝_1 and 𝑝_2). ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">23</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma24" title="Lemma 24. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">24</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma25" title="Lemma 25. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">25</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_term_one}}+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\text{Lemma \ref{lem:p_expectation}}+\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_norm_2}}-2\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:bias_zero_exp}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Similar to <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, adding them together and dividing by <math id="A4.SS5.SSS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we get</p>
<table id="A4.EGx51" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex247"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex247.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\tilde{n}}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left((\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})^{2}+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right)^{2}+\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+\frac{\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\tilde{n}}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left((\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})^{2}+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right)^{2}+\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+\frac{\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex248"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex248.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+o\left(\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\right)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n^{2}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+o\left(\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\right)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n^{2}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.2 </span>Step 4: Variance</h4>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that for the variance, we have the following expression (Section <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS2" title="D.3.2 Variance ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<table id="A4.EGx52" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex249"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex249.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mover accent="true"><mi>n</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.0pt\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{1}{\tilde{n}}\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{int}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{A}}}\right\|_{F}^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex249.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left[\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{z}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mi>𝒁</mi><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝑨</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left[\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{z}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex250"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex250.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\frac{2\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}\alpha_{z}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒁</mi><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>τ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mi>𝜺</mi><mo>]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\frac{2\tilde{\tau}^{2}\alpha_{A}\alpha_{z}}{d}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\frac{\tilde{\tau}^{2}}{d}{\bm{\varepsilon}}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{\varepsilon}}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">In particular that the expectation will be the weighted sum of the expressions from Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma26" title="Lemma 26. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma27" title="Lemma 27. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma28" title="Lemma 28. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma29" title="Lemma 29. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a>. Informally,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex251" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex251.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left(\alpha_{Z}^{2}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:interaction_ZZ}}+2\alpha_{Z}\alpha_{A}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:interaction_AZ}}+\alpha_{A}^{2}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:interaction_AA}}+\text{Lemma \ref{lem:epsilon_term}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma26" title="Lemma 26. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma28" title="Lemma 28. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">28</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma27" title="Lemma 27. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">27</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mtext>Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#Thmlemma29" title="Lemma 29. ‣ D.5.6 Variance: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">29</span></a></mtext></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left(\alpha_{Z}^{2}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:interaction_ZZ}}+2\alpha_{Z}\alpha_{A}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:interaction_AZ}}+\alpha_{A}^{2}\times\text{Lemma \ref{lem:interaction_AA}}+\text{Lemma \ref{lem:epsilon_term}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">This yields that for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, after simplification, the variance is</p>
<table id="A4.EGx53" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex252"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex252.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left[\alpha_{A}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})^{2}\frac{\eta^{2}(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}+2\alpha_{A}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}\right]\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left[\alpha_{A}^{2}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})^{2}\frac{\eta^{2}(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}+2\alpha_{A}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}\right]\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex253"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex253.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\quad+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\left(\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{d}{\rho^{2}}-\frac{\eta^{2}}{\rho^{2}(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}\right)\right]+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\quad+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\left(\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{d}{\rho^{2}}-\frac{\eta^{2}}{\rho^{2}(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}\right)\right]+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS5.SSS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we similarly simplify it to:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx54" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex254"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex254.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left[\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\left(\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{c}-\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\right)+({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left[\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}\left(\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{c}-\frac{\alpha_{A}^{2}}{d}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\right)+({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex255"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex255.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.\quad+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\left(\frac{d}{\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}-\frac{\eta^{2}}{\rho^{2}(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})}\frac{c}{c-1}\right)\right]+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>τ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>d</mi><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.\quad+\tau_{\varepsilon}^{2}\left(\frac{d}{\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}-\frac{\eta^{2}}{\rho^{2}(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})}\frac{c}{c-1}\right)\right]+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS3" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.3 </span>Step 4: Data Noise</h4>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall that for the data noise, we have the following expression</p>
<table id="A4.Ex256" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex256.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\tilde{\alpha}_{A}^{2}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Noting that <math id="A4.SS5.SSS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}=\Theta(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}=\Theta(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we see that this term has no more randomness and we do not need to estimate anything.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS4" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.4 </span>Step 4: Target Alignment</h4>

<div id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Recall from Section <a href="#A4.SS3.SSS4" title="D.3.4 Target Alignment ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3.4</span></a> that the alignment is given by</p>
<table id="A4.Ex257" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex257.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\mathbb{E}\left[\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\mathbb{E}\left[\alpha_{z}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+\alpha_{A}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">From <a href="#Thmlemma30" title="Lemma 30. ‣ D.5.7 Target Alignment: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">30</span></a>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex258" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex258.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\begin{cases}\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\rho^{2}+\eta^{2}c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)&amp;c&lt;1\\
\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\begin{cases}\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\rho^{2}+\eta^{2}c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)&amp;c&lt;1\\
\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and from <a href="#Thmlemma31" title="Lemma 31. ‣ D.5.7 Target Alignment: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">31</span></a>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx55" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex259"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex259.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\begin{cases}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}-\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\rho^{2}+\eta^{2}c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right),&amp;c&lt;1\\
\frac{1}{c}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}-\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\left(\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}+\frac{1}{c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right)+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right),&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\begin{cases}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}-\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\rho^{2}+\eta^{2}c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right),&amp;c&lt;1\\
\frac{1}{c}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}-\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\left(\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}+\frac{1}{c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right)+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right),&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.4" class="ltx_p">Thus for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, the entire interaction term now becomes</p>
<table id="A4.Ex260" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex260.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left(\alpha_{A}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\,({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\,\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\rho^{2}+\eta^{2}c}+o(1)\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left(\alpha_{A}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\,({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\,\frac{\eta^{2}c}{\rho^{2}+\eta^{2}c}+o(1)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.5" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A4.SS5.SSS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, instead we have</p>
<table id="A4.EGx56" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex261"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex261.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{d}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>ρ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\frac{2\tilde{\alpha}_{A}\tilde{\rho}^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{d}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}+\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS5" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.5 </span>Bias: Helper Lemmas</h4>

<div id="Thmlemma22" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma22.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 22</span></span><span id="Thmlemma22.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma22.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma22.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma22.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the same setting as <a href="#S2" title="2 Problem Setting ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have that for <math id="Thmlemma22.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx57" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex262"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex262.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right)^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right)^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex263"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex263.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex263.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmlemma22.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma22.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For <math id="Thmlemma22.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx58" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex264"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex264.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex265"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex265.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex265.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\!\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right]^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\!\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right]^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, we first expand the square and get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex266" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex266.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right)^{2}=(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})^{2}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\frac{\eta^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})^{2}+\frac{2}{\eta}\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right)^{2}=(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})^{2}+\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\frac{\eta^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})^{2}+\frac{2}{\eta}\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma20" title="Lemma 20 (Moments of 𝜂^4/𝛾_𝑖^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, then we see that, using the square root of the covariance to bound the difference between the expectation of the product and the product of the expectation.</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx59" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex267"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex267.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex267.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex268"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex268.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex269"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex269.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{2}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{2}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex270"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex270.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{1}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta\xi}{\gamma_{1}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex270.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex271"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex271.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex272"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex272.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Combining these terms together, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx60" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex273"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex273.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right)^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{1}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right)^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex274"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex274.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex274.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})^{2}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{2}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\right)(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})^{2}\right." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})^{2}+\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{2}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\right)(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})^{2}\right.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex275"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex275.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\left.+\frac{2\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta}\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\right)(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mi>o</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>O</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left.+\frac{2\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta}\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)\right)(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex276"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex276.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex276.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\eta n}\right)\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}(\alpha_{Z}-\alpha_{A})\right]^{2}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\eta n}\right)\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We now consider <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>. Recalling that <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, we let <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> and expand:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex277"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex277.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex278"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex278.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex278.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex279"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex279.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex279.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]{\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]{\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex280"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex280.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex280.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle c_{1}^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\tilde{\eta}^{2}\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}((\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+2c_{1}\tilde{\eta}^{2}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle c_{1}^{2}\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\tilde{\eta}^{2}\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}((\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}+2c_{1}\tilde{\eta}^{2}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">Not that for the second and third terms, we have that <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi,\gamma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi,\gamma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> only depend on the singular values of <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑨</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the rest only depend on the singular vectors. Hence, these terms are independent.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">First note that when <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d&gt;n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d&gt;n</annotation></semantics></math>, the number of singular values equals <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>, which is less than the dimension <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result,</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex281" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex281.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}}^{\top}{\bm{V}}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}{\bm{U}}^{\top}={\bm{U}}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{I}}_{n\times n}\quad\bm{0}_{n\times(d-n)}\\
\bm{0}_{(d-n)\times n}\quad\bm{0}_{(d-n)\times(d-n)}\end{bmatrix}{\bm{U}}^{\top}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝚺</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑽</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑽</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝚺</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝑼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑼</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}={\bm{U}}{\bm{\Sigma}}{\bm{V}}^{\top}{\bm{V}}{\bm{\Sigma}}^{\dagger}{\bm{U}}^{\top}={\bm{U}}\begin{bmatrix}{\bm{I}}_{n\times n}\quad\bm{0}_{n\times(d-n)}\\
\bm{0}_{(d-n)\times n}\quad\bm{0}_{(d-n)\times(d-n)}\end{bmatrix}{\bm{U}}^{\top}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{U}})_{i}^{2}\right]=\frac{n}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{c}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑼</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\right]=\sum_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{U}})_{i}^{2}\right]=\frac{n}{d}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{c}\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">since <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑼</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a uniformly random vector of length <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|</annotation></semantics></math> in <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> after the rotation <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{U}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝑼</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{U}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">For the middle term, by Proposition <a href="#Thmprop2" title="Proposition 2. ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and the above Equation <a href="#A4.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ Proof. ‣ D.5.5 Bias: Helper Lemmas ‣ D.5 Step 4: Bounding the Expectation of Products of Dependent Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx62" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex282"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex282.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}((\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mo>[</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>𝑨</mi><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒖</mi><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>𝑨</mi><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}((\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex283"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex283.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex283.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\alpha_{Z}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}-2\alpha_{A}\alpha_{Z}\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\alpha_{A}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\alpha_{Z}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}-2\alpha_{A}\alpha_{Z}\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\alpha_{A}^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex284"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex284.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\ " display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>=</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\ </annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex284.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for the last term, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex285" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex285.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}){\bm{u}}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus putting these expectations together, we get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx63" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex286"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex286.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[c_{1}^{2}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}+2c_{1}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right]\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[c_{1}^{2}+\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)^{2}+2c_{1}\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right]\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex286.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[c_{1}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right]^{2}\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[c_{1}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right]^{2}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Similar to the <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> case, we take the expectation for terms involving <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> and get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx64" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex287"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex287.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[\left((\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\!\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right)^{\!2}+o\!\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\!\left(\frac{1}{\eta n}\right)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.315em;" width="0.315em"><mi>o</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi>O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\eta}^{2}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left[\left((\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z})+\frac{\rho^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\!\left(\alpha_{Z}-\frac{\alpha_{A}}{c}\right)\right)^{\!2}+o\!\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\right)+O\!\left(\frac{1}{\eta n}\right)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma23" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma23.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 23</span></span><span id="Thmlemma23.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Expectations involving <math id="Thmlemma23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmlemma23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmlemma23.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma23.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma23.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma23.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting of <a href="#S2" title="2 Problem Setting ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I13" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I13.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I13.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I13.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I13.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I13.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=d/n&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=d/n&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I13.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex288" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex288.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}\right]=\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}\right]=\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I13.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I13.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I13.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I13.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For </span><math id="A4.I13.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c=d/n&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c=d/n&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I13.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex289" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex289.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}\right]=\frac{\eta^{2}}{c-1}\,\frac{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}\right]=\frac{\eta^{2}}{c-1}\,\frac{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">First, Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6 (Squared Norms of 𝒑_1 and 𝒑_2). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> tells us that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex290" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex290.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}=\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}=\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Then recall from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex291" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex291.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]=\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}]=\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2})=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.3.1" class="ltx_text">and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma19" title="Lemma 19 (Moments of 𝜂^2/𝛾_𝑖). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> tells us</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex292" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex292.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{i}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]=\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{i}}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p5.4.1" class="ltx_text">Again Section <a href="#A4.SS4.SSS2" title="D.4.2 Step 3(b): Bounding the Higher Moments ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.4.2</span></a> tells us that the assumption of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a> is satisfied and that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx65" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex293"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex293.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{1}\|^{2}\right]=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex293.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{1}}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex294"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex294.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex295"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex295.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c}{1-c}\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.1" class="ltx_p">Using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6 (Squared Norms of 𝒑_1 and 𝒑_2). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> for <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{p}}_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{p}}_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A4.Ex296" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex296.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\left(\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}+2\eta^{3}\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}+\eta^{2}\xi^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}=\frac{1}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\left(\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}+2\eta^{3}\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}+\eta^{2}\xi^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.2" class="ltx_p">To begin, we start estimating</p>
<table id="A4.Ex297" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex297.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.3" class="ltx_p">Using our Spherical Hypercontractivity, we have that <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy the assumptions for Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma36" title="Lemma 36 (Variance of general product). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>. Then using Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> and <a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 (General Terms). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> we first have that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex298" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex298.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]=1-\frac{1}{c}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{d}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]=1-\frac{1}{c}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.Ex299" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex299.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]=\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c^{3}}{(c-1)^{3}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{8}d}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]=\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c^{3}}{(c-1)^{3}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{8}d}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.4" class="ltx_p">Thus, using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx66" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex300"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex300.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex300.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]+O\left(\max\left(\frac{1}{d},\frac{1}{\rho^{8}d}\right)\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>8</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]+O\left(\max\left(\frac{1}{d},\frac{1}{\rho^{8}d}\right)\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex301"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex301.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(1-\frac{1}{c}\right)^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c^{3}}{(c-1)^{3}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(1-\frac{1}{c}\right)^{2}\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c^{3}}{(c-1)^{3}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex302"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex302.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.5" class="ltx_p">and using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma36" title="Lemma 36 (Variance of general product). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>, since all the means are <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex303" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex303.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)=O\left(\max\left(\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right),\mathrm{Var}\left({\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)\right)\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)=O\left(\max\left(\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right),\mathrm{Var}\left({\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)\right)\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.6" class="ltx_p">Then Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma20" title="Lemma 20 (Moments of 𝜂^4/𝛾_𝑖^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> gives mean and variance of <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{i}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{i}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math> does not satisfy the higher moment bound, and cannot be directly included in the product, we can include it via the classical bound:</p>
<table id="A4.EGx67" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.E14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>Var</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}{\bm{h}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\frac{c}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.7" class="ltx_p">Similarly, we can do the same thing for the other term. For the middle term we note that from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma11" title="Lemma 11 (Zero Expectation). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></p>
<table id="A4.Ex304" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex304.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]=0\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left({\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{6}d}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>6</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]=0\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left({\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{6}d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.8" class="ltx_p">and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> tells us</p>
<table id="A4.Ex305" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex305.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]=1-\frac{1}{c}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{d}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]=1-\frac{1}{c}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.9" class="ltx_p">and</p>
<table id="A4.Ex306" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex306.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]=\frac{1}{\eta}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext> and </mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]=\frac{1}{\eta}\quad\text{ and }\quad\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.10" class="ltx_p">Thus using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.Ex307" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex307.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]=0+O\left(\frac{1}{d}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]=0+O\left(\frac{1}{d}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.11" class="ltx_p">Thus using the standard covariance bound for the expectation of product versus product of expectation, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx68" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex308"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex308.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{3}\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{3}\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex308.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=0+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=0+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.12" class="ltx_p">For the last term, we have that, using Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a></p>
<table id="A4.EGx69" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex309"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex309.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex309.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}\cdot\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex310"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex310.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.13" class="ltx_p">and from Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma36" title="Lemma 36 (Variance of general product). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a></p>
<table id="A4.Ex311" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex311.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.14" class="ltx_p">Then using the standard bound, we have that</p>
<table id="A4.EGx70" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex312"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex312.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\xi^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\xi^{2}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex312.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒌</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\|{\bm{k}}\|^{2}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex313"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex313.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\frac{1}{c-1}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{4}n}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex314"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex314.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.15" class="ltx_p">Finally, putting all three terms together we get</p>
<table id="A4.EGx71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex315"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex315.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝒑</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\|{\bm{p}}_{2}\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex315.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+\frac{1}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{c}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+\frac{1}{c-1}\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}\eta^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex316"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex316.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\eta^{2}}{c-1}\,\frac{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\eta^{2}}{c-1}\,\frac{\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p6.16" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7.1" class="ltx_p">From the above proofs, we make an important observation that the individual terms from Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 (General Terms). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma11" title="Lemma 11 (Zero Expectation). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma16" title="Lemma 16 (Moments of 𝛾_𝑖/𝜂^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> all have means <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1)</annotation></semantics></math> and variances <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/n)</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, by Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma36" title="Lemma 36 (Variance of general product). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>, we can bound the variance of a product of terms by <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(1/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(1/n)</annotation></semantics></math>, given that these terms satisfy the lemma assumptions. Essentially, only <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{2}/\gamma_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{2}/\gamma_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS5.SSS5.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\eta^{4}/\gamma_{i}^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\eta^{4}/\gamma_{i}^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> fail the assumption on higher moment bound, so we deal with them via the classical bound after carrying out the product. This simplification ensures proper concentration and will be used at times in the following proofs without reference.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS5.SSS6" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">D.5.6 </span>Variance: Helper Lemmas</h4>

<div id="Thmlemma24" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma24.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 24</span></span><span id="Thmlemma24.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma24.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma24.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma24.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting of <a href="#S2" title="2 Problem Setting ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have that for <math id="Thmlemma24.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex317" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex317.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}\right]=\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|\beta_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}\right]=\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|\beta_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx72" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex318"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex318.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex318.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}=\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}=\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text">Similar to last lemma, using Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 (General Terms). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma20" title="Lemma 20 (Moments of 𝜂^4/𝛾_𝑖^2). ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a>, we get</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex319"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex319.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex319.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\right)^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex320"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex320.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\rho^{2}+\eta^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(1-\frac{1}{c}\right)^{2}\left(\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\frac{c}{\rho^{2}(c-1)}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}d}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\rho^{2}+\eta^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(1-\frac{1}{c}\right)^{2}\left(\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\frac{c}{\rho^{2}(c-1)}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}d}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex321"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex321.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{4}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\|{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{4}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, it directly follows from here that</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex322"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex322.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒖</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\left\|\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}^{\top}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\right\|^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex322.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{s}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{h}}^{\top}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex323"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex323.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|\beta_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>c</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}^{2}\frac{\|\beta_{*}\|^{2}}{d}\left(\frac{c-1}{c}\right)\frac{\eta^{2}\rho^{2}}{(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma25" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma25.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 25</span></span><span id="Thmlemma25.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma25.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma25.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma25.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the setting of <a href="#S2" title="2 Problem Setting ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have that for <math id="Thmlemma25.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;1</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex324" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex324.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑰</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}\left[(\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}){\bm{I}}+\frac{\xi}{\gamma_{2}}(\alpha_{Z}{\bm{I}}-\alpha_{A}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger})\right]\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒗</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\bm{Z}}}=\tilde{\eta}{\bm{u}}\tilde{{\bm{v}}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, we can expand this into three terms. We can take expectations in a similar way via Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma9" title="Lemma 9 (Generalized version of Lemma 7 from []). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma10" title="Lemma 10 (General Terms). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma11" title="Lemma 11 (Zero Expectation). ‣ D.4.1 Step 3(a): Showing that basic building blocks concentrate ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>: Let <math id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}=\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>α</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}=\tilde{\alpha}_{Z}-\alpha_{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>. Each term contains a zero expectation:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx75" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex325"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex325.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}c_{1}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}c_{1}\frac{\eta\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex325.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta}c_{1}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta}c_{1}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex326"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex326.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta}c_{1}\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)=O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msub><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>η</mi><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta}c_{1}\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{2}}{\gamma_{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)=O\left(\frac{\eta}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.EGx76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex327"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex327.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{Z}\frac{\eta\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{Z}\frac{\eta\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex327.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex328"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex328.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A4.EGx77" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex329"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex329.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\tilde{\eta}^{2}\alpha_{A}\frac{\eta\xi\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex329.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ξ</mi><mi>η</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒔</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi}{\eta}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{s}}\|^{2}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{A}}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{u}}{\bm{h}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex330"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex330.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>Z</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi>η</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\alpha_{Z}\tilde{\eta}^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\left(\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{2}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}\right)=O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus the cross term concentrates around zero at a rate of <math id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\eta/n)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>η</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\eta/n)</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma26" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma26.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 26</span></span><span id="Thmlemma26.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma26.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma26.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma26.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In the same setting as <a href="#S2" title="2 Problem Setting ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, we have that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex331" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex331.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\begin{cases}\frac{\eta^{2}(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)&amp;c&lt;1\\
\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{c-1}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>c</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\left[{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}\right]=\begin{cases}\frac{\eta^{2}(\eta^{2}+\rho^{2})}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o(1)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)&amp;c&lt;1\\
\frac{\eta^{2}}{\eta^{2}+\rho^{2}}\frac{c}{c-1}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)&amp;c&gt;1\end{cases}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start with <math id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math> and expand this term using Proposition <a href="#Thmprop1" title="Proposition 1 (Proposition 2 from []). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex332" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex332.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}=\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}({\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{k}})({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{2\eta^{3}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\xi}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒁</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑨</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mrow><mo>†</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⊤</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒌</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒕</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒌</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>†</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝒉</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{Z}}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger}({\bm{Z}}+{\bm{A}})^{\dagger\top}{\bm{Z}}{\bm{\beta}}_{*}=\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{\eta^{4}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}({\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger\top}{\bm{k}})({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}+\frac{2\eta^{3}\|{\bm{t}}\|^{2}\xi}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}{\bm{k}}^{\top}{\bm{A}}^{\dagger}{\bm{h}}^{\top}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">We then start plugging in the expectations of these three terms and the “cumulative" variance of the sum according to Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma37" title="Lemma 37 (Expectation of Product vs. Product of Expectations). ‣ Appendix E Probability Lemmas ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">37</span></a>.</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx78" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex333"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex333.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{2}\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}\xi^{2}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex333.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>ξ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒉</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>γ</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>O</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\frac{\xi^{2}}{\eta^{2}}\right]\mathbb{E}\left[\|{\bm{h}}\|^{2}\right]+\sqrt{\mathrm{Var}\left(\frac{\eta^{4}}{\gamma_{1}^{2}}\right)O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex334"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex334.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝜷</mi><mo>∗</mo><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒖</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>η</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msup><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>o</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=({\bm{\beta}}_{*}^{\top}{\bm{u}})^{2}\left(\frac{\rho^{4}\eta^{4}}{(\eta^{2}c+\rho^{2})^{2}}+o(1)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\eta^{2}}+O\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}n}\right)\right)\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\frac{c^{2}}{1-c}+o\left(\frac{1}{\rho^{2}}\right)\right)+O\left(\frac{1}{n}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex335"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
