<p id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS5.SSS6.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">By the squared norms in Lemmas <a href="#Thmlemma6" title="Lemma 6 (Squared Norms of 𝒑_1 and 𝒑_2). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#Thmlemma7" title="Lemma 7 (Squared Norms of 𝒒_1 and 𝒒_2). ‣ D.3.5 Helper Lemmas ‣ D.3 Step 2: Simplifying Terms ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, and Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma21" title="Lemma 21. ‣ D.4.3 Step 3(c): Bounding 𝛾_𝑖 moments. ‣ D.4 Step 3: Random Matrix Theory Estimates ‣ Appendix D Proof of Theorem ‣ Risk Phase Transitions in Spiked Regression: Alignment Driven Benign and Catastrophic Overfitting" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>,</span></p>
